**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
*.log

# --- 2026-08-31 CVE sweep: keep dev/CI-only artifacts OUT of the build context ---
# `COPY . .` in the build stage swept these into the shipped image, where a scanner
# then found their (irrelevant-at-runtime) CVEs and their bytes were pure attack surface.
#
# .claude — Claude Code's working dir. It holds LINKED GIT WORKTREES of other sessions
# (.claude/worktrees/*), so `COPY . .` was dragging ~190 MiB of a second, third, … full
# checkout — each carrying its own committed tools/openapi/bin/oasdiff Go binary — into
# the image. Never needed by the build or at runtime.
.claude
# The oasdiff Go binary is the /v1 breaking-change gate — a BUILD/CI tool (pnpm gen),
# never read at runtime (the server emits its OpenAPI from Zod in-process). Its old Go
# stdlib carried several CRITICAL/HIGH CVEs. tools/openapi/openapi.v1.json (the spec
# itself) is kept — only the binary is excluded.
tools/openapi/bin
# CI workflow definitions — never part of the runtime image.
.github
